  "uncertainties": [
    "Moonlit Guidance copies the selected original deck card with current stored material. Existing per-face offering samples a physical representative once; exact CN duplicate weights remain deferred.",
    "A successfully delivered copy arms only its original same-turn hand residence and completed physical play. The accepted original deck reference is drawn normally; stale, transformed or reentered originals are not substituted, and a full hand burns normally. No second choice/discovery is created by this draw.",
    "Volume Up snapshots Finale from its own paid play mana_after value; automatic casts have no paid Finale. Three actual matching spell root attempts define the group; reaction draws and replacement leaves do not become additional options.",
    "Each physical drawn spell keeps an option, including duplicate faces. A still-resident original is copied with current material at group completion; a departed, burned or drawn-cast original falls back to its complete pre-draw material. Exact official copy timing and duplicate display policy remain uncalibrated."
